---
import InfoPageLayout from '../layouts/InfoPageLayout.astro';
import { VIDEO_GAME_JSON_LD } from '../siteMeta';

const title = 'Mystery Emblem: A Pokémon x Fire Emblem Fan Game You Can Play in Your Browser';
const description =
  'Mystery Emblem is a free Pokémon Fire Emblem fan game: grid tactics in the style of Fire Emblem, with Pokémon Mystery Dungeon pixel art. No download, plays on phone and PC.';
---

<InfoPageLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  heading="About Mystery Emblem"
  jsonLd={[VIDEO_GAME_JSON_LD]}
>
  <figure class="info-figure">
    <img
      src="/boxart.webp"
      width="1024"
      height="572"
      alt="Mystery Emblem: Echoes of the Dragon Lineage box art, with Piplup and Flabébé facing a frozen mountain"
      decoding="async"
    />
  </figure>

  <p>
    <strong>Mystery Emblem</strong> is a free <strong>Pokémon x Fire Emblem fan game</strong>. It plays
    like a classic Fire Emblem tactics RPG (move your team across a grid, plan every attack, and
    protect your leader) and looks like <strong>Pokémon Mystery Dungeon: Explorers of Sky</strong>,
    with pixel-art sprites, emotion portraits, and the familiar blue menu windows.
  </p>
  <p>
    It runs right in your web browser on phone, tablet, or PC. There is nothing to download or
    install, and the current demo takes about an hour to finish.
  </p>

  <h2>What kind of game is it?</h2>
  <p>
    A turn-based <strong>strategy RPG</strong>. On your turn you move each Pokémon and choose an attack,
    a heal, or an item. Then the enemy moves. Pokémon types replace Fire Emblem's weapon triangle, and
    Pokémon moves take the place of swords, lances, and magic: physical moves strike up close, and
    special moves hit from range.
  </p>

  <h2>Features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A short personality quiz, in the spirit of Pokémon Mystery Dungeon, picks your hero: Axew, Bagon, Gible, Dratini, or Goomy.</li>
    <li>Fire Emblem-style battles with counterattacks, type advantages, terrain cover, and boss fights.</li>
    <li>Recruit new Pokémon in battle by talking to them, and evolve your team with Evolution Stones.</li>
    <li>A story told through Mystery Dungeon-style cutscenes with character portraits.</li>
    <li>A world map with main chapters, optional side chapters, and Kecleon's traveling shops.</li>
    <li>Sign in with Google to save your progress and continue on any device.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The story</h2>
  <p>
    Long ago, the Dragon Kingdom kept a rift called the Abyss sealed. Then the royal tactician Gengar
    betrayed it, and now the Abyss is spreading and wild Pokémon are turning Feral. You play a young
    Dragon raised in a quiet coastal village by the knight Sir Empoleon. When the Ironscale Empire
    marches on your home, you and your friends set out to warn the King. Meet the cast on the
    <a href="/characters/">Characters</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>What's in the demo</h2>
  <p>
    The current demo, <em>Part 1: The Verdant Heartland</em>, includes the Prologue, six main chapters,
    and two optional side chapters. At the end there's a short feedback form. Every response helps
    shape the full game.
  </p>

  <h2>Who made it?</h2>
  <p>
    Mystery Emblem is a passion project by Adam Kenawell, a longtime fan of both series. Development
    updates are posted on the <a href="https://adam.kenawell.family/blog/">blog</a>. New to tactics
    games? Start with <a href="/how-to-play/">How to Play</a>, or check the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a>.
  </p>
</InfoPageLayout>
